    "updated_at": "2022-02-16T09:17:01Z",
    "body": "Not sure if here is the place, but I think it would be great to also have tests against more random inputs, e.g\r\na single-radius version of https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/canvas/element/path-objects/2d.path.roundrect.nonfinite.html\r\nAnd maybe some additions like\r\n```js\r\nctx.roundRect(x, y, w, h, { foo: \"bar\" }); //=> DOMPointInit with all default values: draws a rect with no rounded border, \r\nctx.roundRect(x, y, w, h, undefined); //=> unrestricted double (NaN) doesn't draw\r\n```\r\nEven previous tests could also benefit from things like\r\n```js\r\nctx.roundRect(x, y, w, h, [[]]); //=>   « unrestricted double (0) »: draws a rect with no rounded border\r\nctx.roundRect(x, y, w, h, [[25]]); //=> « unrestricted double (25) »: draws a \"circle\"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
